cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use gtellcorr, please cite the paper below and the software version you used."
title: "gtellcorr"
type: software
version: 0.10.0
date-released: 2026-10-17
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/xiangluo0902/gtellcorr"
abstract: >-
  Clean the Earth's atmosphere out of your high-resolution spectra. gtellcorr
  rebuilds the atmosphere above your telescope for every exposure, models its
  absorption with LBLRTM, and fits it alongside your star's own lines. The
  molecular columns, the instrumental resolution and the continuum are fitted
  with either a stellar-line mask or a stellar template, and the optical depths
  are cached so that fitting stays fast.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - spectroscopy
  - telluric correction
  - LBLRTM
  - high-resolution spectroscopy
